hadiths[2856]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character.”"
"2","The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character."
"3","Whoever loves to find the sweetness of faith, let him love a person only for the sake of Allah."
"4","A little bit of showing off is shirk (associating partners with Allah), and whoever shows enmity to a friend of Allah has declared war against Allah. Indeed Allah loves the righteous, pious, hidden ones, who if they are absent are not missed, and if they are present are not recognized. Their hearts are the lamps of guidance; they emerge from every dark and dusty place."
"5","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, *""""Īmān (faith) wears out (deteriorates) within ˹the depths˺ of each one of you just as worn out clothing has been worn out. Therefore, ask Allah to renew Īmān in your hearts.""""*[^1]"
"6","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When the servant ˹of Allah˺ commits a sin, a black spot appears upon his heart. If he repents, it is polished away. But if he repeats, ˹the black spot˺ increases until it grows large in his heart. That is the """"rān"""" that Allah mentions in His Book: “Nay! But on their hearts is the rān...” [Muṭaffifīn 83:14][^1]"
"7","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) continued to be asked about the Hour until the verse was revealed: 'In what [position] are you that you should mention it? To your Lord is its finality.' (An-Nazi'at: 44)"
"8","When the servant says: 'There is no god but Allah and Allah is the Greatest,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken the truth. There is no god but Me, and I am Alone.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken the truth. There is no god but Me, and I have no partner.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken the truth. There is no god but Me, to Me belongs the dominion and to Me belongs all praise.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and there is no power and no strength except by Allah,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken the truth. There is no power and no strength except by Me.'"
"9","Indeed Allah will single out a man from my Ummah before all creation on the Day of Resurrection, and will spread out for him ninety-nine scrolls, each scroll as far as the eye can see. Then He will say: 'Do you deny any of this? Have My recording angels wronged you?' He will say: 'No, O Lord.' He will say: 'Do you have any excuse?' He will say: 'No, O Lord.' He will say: 'Rather, you have a good deed with Us, and you will not be wronged today.' Then a card will be brought out containing: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' He will say: 'O Lord, what is this card compared to these scrolls?' He will say: 'You will not be wronged.' The scrolls will be placed in one pan of the scale, and the card in the other. The scrolls will fly up (become light), and the card will weigh heavy. Nothing weighs heavy with the Name of Allah."
"10","The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, the Christians likewise, and my Ummah will split into seventy-three sects."
"11","The covenant between us and them is the prayer; whoever abandons it has disbelieved."
"12","The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not consider the abandonment of any deed as disbelief except the prayer."
"13","Whoever commits a hadd offense and Allah hastens his punishment in this world, Allah is too Just to repeat the punishment upon His servant in the Hereafter. And whoever commits a hadd offense and Allah conceals it and pardons him, Allah is too Generous to return to something He has pardoned."
"14","A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) leading a horse with a foal following it. He asked: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am a Prophet.' He asked: 'What is a Prophet?' He said: 'Messenger of Allah.' He asked: 'When is the Hour?' The Prophet said: 'It is unseen, none knows the unseen except Allah.' He asked: 'Show me your sword.' The Prophet gave him his sword. The man shook it and returned it. The Prophet said: 'Indeed you were not able to do what you intended.' The man said: 'It happened...' The Prophet said: 'Go to him and ask him about these traits.'"
"15","Whoever goes to a fortune-teller or soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"16","There is no soul on earth that dies without associating anything with Allah, testifying that I am the Messenger of Allah, with that returning to a certain heart, except that Allah will forgive it."
"17","Shyness and hesitation in speech are two branches of Iman, ˹while˺ crudeness and ˹bluntness˺ are two branches of hypocrisy."""""
"18","Al-Badhadhah (simplicity/humility) is part of faith, Al-Badhadhah is part of faith."
"19","Worship your Lord, pray your five prayers, fast your month, pay the zakat of your wealth, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord."
"20","A Jew said to his companion: 'Let us go to this Prophet and ask him about this verse: {And We certainly gave Moses nine evident signs} (Al-Isra: 101). His companion said: 'Do not say he is a Prophet, for if he hears you, it will become four eyes for him.' So they asked him. The Prophet said: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, do not practice magic, do not consume usury, do not walk with an innocent person to a ruler to have him killed, do not accuse a chaste woman, and you Jews specifically: do not transgress in the Sabbath.' They kissed his hand and foot and said: 'We bear witness that you are a Prophet.' He said: 'What prevented you from accepting Islam?' They said: 'David (peace be upon him) prayed that there would always be a Prophet from his descendants, and we fear the Jews would kill us.'"
"21","By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe! They said: 'And what is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'A neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his mischief.' They said: 'What is his mischief?' He said: 'His evil.'"
"22","The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the Believer is the one whom people trust with their lives and wealth."
"23","The most complete of the believers is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"24","Shall I not inform you of the Believer? The one whom people trust with their lives and wealth. And the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. And the Mujahid is the one who strives against his soul in obedience. And the Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who abandons sins and transgressions."
"25","The Believer is the one whom people trust. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The Muhajir is the one who abandons evil. And the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant enters Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his mischief."
"26","Beware of oppression, for oppression is darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of obscenity and shamelessness. Beware of stinginess, for those before you were destroyed by stinginess. It commanded them to cut ties and they cut them, to be miserly and they were miserly, to be immoral and they were immoral. A man stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best?' He said: 'That the Muslims are safe from your tongue and hand.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which hijrah (emigration) is best?' He said: 'To abandon what your Lord dislikes.' And hijrah is of two types: the hijrah of the city-dweller and the hijrah of the bedouin. The hijrah of the bedouin: to respond when called and obey when commanded. The hijrah of the city-dweller is greater in hardship and greater in reward."
"27","Fear oppression, then he mentioned the hadith at length. (Similar to Hadith 26)"
"28","Beware of obscenity and shamelessness, for Allah does not love the obscene and shameless. Beware of oppression, for it is darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of stinginess, for it called those before you and they shed their blood, it called those before you and they cut their family ties, it called those before you and they made lawful their sacred things."
"29","The Believer is not a slanderer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor vulgar."
"30","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us: from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi: from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: from his father: from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"The believer is not a slanderer (ta'yan), nor a curser (la'an), nor obscene (fahish), nor vulgar (badhi)."""" """"And this hadith has a second witness, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, which must be mentioned even though its chain is not on the condition of the two Shaykhs (Bukhari and Muslim)."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 30 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis.There is another witness regarding this hadith from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i. It must be mentioned, even if its chain of transmission does not meet the conditions of the two Sheikhs."
"31","Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mati informed us in Kufa: al-Husayn ibn al-Hakim al-Hiri narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us: Sabah ibn Yahya narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Layla: from al-Hakam: from Ibrahim: from Alqamah: from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: """"The believer is not a slanderer, nor obscene, nor vulgar."""" """"Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, even though he is attributed with poor memory, is one of the jurists of Islam and their virtuous ones, and from the elders of the children of the Companions and the Followers from the Ansar, may Allah's mercy be upon them."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 31 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"32","Abu Muhammad Da'laq ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated to us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sayigh narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: from Amr, mawla of al-Muttalib: from al-Muttalib: from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Whoever does a bad deed and hates it when he does it, and does a good deed and rejoices in it, he is a believer."""" """"They have cited the narrators of this hadith, the last of them, and it is authentic on their condition, but they did not output it; rather they output it in the sermon of Umar ibn al-Khattab: 'Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed, he is a believer,' and it has a witness with this wording."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 32 - On the condition of the two (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"33","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qadi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: from Zayd ibn Salam: from his grandfather Mamtur: from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked by a man, who said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith (iman)? He said: """"When your good deed pleases you and your bad deed grieves you, then you are a believer."""" He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sin (ithm)? He said: """"When something troubles your chest, then leave it."""" And thus narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak and Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 33 - Ma'mar and Ali ibn al-Mubarak followed him, and it is on the condition of the two. As for the hadith of Ali ibn al-Mubarak..."
"34","Makram ibn Ahmad al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir informed me: from Zayd ibn Salam: from his grandfather Abu Salam, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): What is faith? He said: """"When your good deed pleases you and your bad deed grieves you, then you are a believer."""" And as for the hadith of Ma'mar..."
"35","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San'ani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: from Zayd ibn Salam: from Abu Salam: from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: What is faith? He said: """"Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed, he is a believer."""" """"All these hadiths are authentic, connected, on the condition of the two Shaykhs."""""
"36","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jabir informed me: he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir say: I heard Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i say: We camped with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at a place, so I woke up at night, and I saw nothing in the camp longer than the rear of my saddle; every person and his camel had stuck to the ground. So I went among the people until I reached the Prophet's (peace be upon him) sleeping place, but he was not in it. I placed my hand on the bedding, and it was cold. So I went out among the people saying: {Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return} [al-Baqarah: 156] - the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has been taken away. Until I went out of the entire camp, I looked at a darkness and threw a stone, and I went to the darkness, and behold, it was Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. And there was a sound before us like the humming of a millstone, or like the sound of pebbles when the wind hits them. Some of us said to others: O people, stay put until morning comes or the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) comes to you. He said: We stayed as Allah willed, then he called out: """"Is there Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and Awf ibn Malik?"""" We said: Yes, indeed. So he came to us, and we walked with him, not asking him about anything nor informing him of anything. He sat on his bedding and said: """"Do you know what my Lord gave me a choice of tonight?"""" We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: """"He gave me a choice between admitting half of my Ummah into Paradise, and intercession. So I chose intercession."""" We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among its people. He said: """"It is for every Muslim."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of Muslim, and they did not output it. Its narrators are all trustworthy on the condition of both of them, and it has no defect. And there is nothing in the other reports of intercession saying 'it is for every Muslim'."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 36 - On the condition of the two."
"37","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us. And Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi informed us in Marw: Ahmad ibn Sayyar narrated to us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us. They said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Najih: from his father: from Ibn Abbas, who said: """"The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) never fought a people until he invited them."""" """"This hadith is authentic from the hadith of al-Thawri, and they did not output it. And Muslim cited Abu Najih, the father of Abdullah, whose name is Yasar, and he is from the mawali of the Meccans."""" And it has been narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with this wording. And they both agreed on outputting the hadith of Abdullah ibn Awn: 'I wrote to Nafi', mawla of Abdullah ibn Umar, asking him about fighting before invitation, so he wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq... the hadith, and in it: the invitation was before the fighting.' [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 37 - Muslim cited Abu Najih Yasar al-Makki."
"38","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ali al-Sirafi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Salama ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us: he heard Rabi'ah ibn Abbad al-Du'ali say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at Mina in their dwellings before he migrated to Medina, saying: """"O people, Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him."""" He said: And behind him was a man saying: """"O people, this man commands you to leave the religion of your fathers."""" So I asked: Who is this man? They said: Abu Lahab. """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, and its narrators to the last of them are trustworthy, reliable. Perhaps they or one of them imagined that Rabi'ah ibn Abbad has no narrator other than Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, and Abu al-Zinad Abdullah ibn Dhakwan has also narrated this exact hadith from him."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 38 - On the condition of the two."
"39","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab informed us, in Hamdan: Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us: my father informed me: Rabi'ah ibn Abbad al-Du'ali informed me: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in the Jahiliyyah at the market of Dhu al-Majaz, and he was saying: """"O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will succeed."""" He said: He repeated it many times, and the people were gathered around him following him. And behind him was a man, cross-eyed, with two braids, bright-faced, saying: """"He is a Sabian, a liar."""" So I asked: Who is this? They said: His uncle, Abu Lahab. """"And I only cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad following them, for they both cited him together."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 39 - Rather I cited Ibn Abi al-Zinad, for they both cited him."
"40","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Salih ibn Rustam narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah: from Aisha, who said: An old woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was with me. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: """"Who are you?"""" She said: I am Jaththamah al-Muzaniyyah. He said: """"Rather you are Hassnah al-Muzaniyyah. How are you? How is your condition? How were you after us?"""" She said: Good, by my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah. When she left, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you turn to this old woman with such attention? He said: """"She used to visit us during Khadijah's time, and keeping good ties is from faith."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, for they agreed on citing its narrators in many hadiths, and it has no defect."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 40 - On the condition of the two and it has no defect."
"41","Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Anbari narrated to us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karabisi informed us: Safwan ibn Salih al-Dimashqi narrated to us. They said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us: from Abu al-Zinad: from al-A'raj: from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. He is Witr (One) and loves the Witr - He is Allah - there is no god but Him: al-Rahman, al-Rahim, al-Malik, al-Quddus, al-Salam, al-Mu'min, al-Muhaymin, al-Aziz, al-Jabbar, al-Mutakabbir, al-Khaliq, al-Bari, al-Musawwir, al-Ghaffar, al-Qahhar, al-Wahhab, al-Razzaq, al-Fattah, al-Alim, al-Qabid, al-Basit, al-Khafid, al-Rafi', al-Mu'izz, al-Mudhill, al-Sami', al-Basir, al-Hakam, al-Adl, al-Latif, al-Khabir, al-Halim, al-Azim, al-Ghafur, al-Shakur, al-Ali, al-Kabir, al-Hafiz, al-Mughith."""" And Safwan said in his hadith: al-Muqit. And to this went Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq in Mukhtasar al-Sahih: al-Hasib, al-Jalil, al-Karim, al-Raqib, al-Mujib, al-Wasi', al-Hakim, al-Wadud, al-Majid, al-Ba'ith, al-Shahid, al-Haqq, al-Wakil, al-Qawiyy, al-Matin, al-Waliyy, al-Hamid, al-Muhsi, al-Mubdi, al-Mu'id, al-Muhyi, al-Mumit, al-Hayy, al-Qayyum, al-Wajid, al-Majid, al-Wahid, al-Samad, al-Qadir, al-Muqtadir, al-Muqaddim, al-Mu'akhkhir, al-Awwal, al-Akhir, al-Zahir, al-Batin, al-Wali, al-Muta'ali, al-Barr, al-Tawwab, al-Muntaqim, al-Afuww, al-Ra'uf, Malik al-Mulk, Dhu al-Jalal wa al-Ikram, al-Muqsit, al-Jami', al-Ghani, al-Mughni, al-Mani', al-Darr, al-Nafi', al-Nur, al-Hadi, al-Badi', al-Baqi, al-Warith, al-Rashid, al-Sabur."""" """"This is a hadith they both output in the two Sahihs with authentic chains, without mentioning the names in it. The defect with them is that al-Walid ibn Muslim singled out narrating it at length, and mentioned the names in it, and no one else mentioned them. And this is not a defect, for I know no difference among the imams of hadith that al-Walid ibn Muslim is more trustworthy, more precise, more knowledgeable, and greater than Abu al-Yaman, Bishr ibn Shu'ayb, Ali ibn Ayyash, and their peers among the companions of Shu'ayb. Then we looked and found the hadith has been narrated by Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Hisham ibn Hassan together, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him) at length."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 41 - They did not output the names due to al-Walid's singularity with them, and that is not a defect, for al-Walid is more trustworthy and precise than Abu al-Yaman and Ali ibn Ayyash."
"42","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab narrated to us, in Hamdan: the Amir Abu al-Haytham Khalid ibn Ahmad al-Duhli narrated to us, in Hamdan: Abu Asad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Balkhi narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani and Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: they said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman narrated to us: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us: from Muhammad ibn Sirin: from Abu Hurayrah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise: Allah, al-Rahman, al-Rahim, al-Ilah, al-Rabb, al-Malik, al-Quddus, al-Salam, al-Mu'min, al-Muhaymin, al-Aziz, al-Jabbar, al-Mutakabbir, al-Khaliq, al-Bari, al-Musawwir, al-Halim, al-Alim, al-Sami', al-Basir, al-Hayy, al-Qayyum, al-Wasi', al-Latif, al-Khabir, al-Hannan, al-Mannan, al-Badi', al-Wadud, al-Ghafur, al-Shakur, al-Majid, al-Mubdi, al-Mu'id, al-Nur, al-Awwal, al-Akhir, al-Zahir, al-Batin, al-Ghaffar, al-Wahhab, al-Qadir, al-Ahad, al-Samad, al-Kafi, al-Baqi, al-Wakil, al-Majid, al-Mughith, al-Da'im, al-Muta'ali, Dhu al-Jalal wa al-Ikram, al-Mawla, al-Nasir, al-Haqq, al-Mubin, al-Ba'ith, al-Mujib, al-Muhyi, al-Mumit, al-Jamil, al-Sadiq, al-Hafiz, al-Kabir, al-Qarib, al-Raqib, al-Fattah, al-Tawwab, al-Qadim, al-Witr, al-Fatir, al-Razzaq, al-Allam, al-Ali, al-Azim, al-Ghani, al-Malik, al-Muqtadir, al-Akram, al-Ra'uf, al-Mudabbir, al-Malik, al-Qadir, al-Hadi, al-Shakir, al-Rafi', al-Shahid, al-Wahid, Dhu al-Tawl, Dhu al-Ma'arij, Dhu al-Fadl, al-Khallaq, al-Kafil, al-Jalil, al-Karim."""" """"This hadith is preserved from the hadith of Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, abbreviated without mentioning the additional names in it. All of them are in the Quran. And Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman is trustworthy, even though they did not output him. And I only made it a witness for the first hadith."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 42 - Rather they weakened him, meaning Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman."
"43","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, in Hamdan: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn Babawaih narrated to us: they said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us: Affan, Muhammad ibn Kathir, and Abu Amr al-Hawzi narrated to us: they said: Shu'bah narrated to us: Salimah ibn Kuhayl informed me: he said: I heard Isa - a man from Banu Asad - narrating, from Zirr: from Abdullah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Superstition (tiyarah) is shirk, but Allah Almighty removes it by trust (tawakkul)."""" """"And this Isa is: Ibn Abi Asim al-Asadi, Kufan, trustworthy."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 43 - Isa ibn Abi Asim is trustworthy."
"44","Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us with the authenticity of what we mentioned: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah informed me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Shu'bah: from Salimah ibn Kuhayl: from Isa ibn Asim: from Zirr: from Abdullah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Superstition is from shirk, and a safe haven, but Allah removes it by trust."""" """"This hadith is authentic in its chain, its narrators are trustworthy, and they did not output it."""" And Isa ibn Asim al-Asadi has also narrated from Adi ibn Thabit and others. And Shu'bah, Jarir ibn Hazim, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih and others have narrated from him."
"45","Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, and Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: they said: Yahya ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Jarir informed us: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah al-Nakha'i: from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Whoever swears by other than Allah has disbelieved."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, for they cited the like of this chain and output it in the Book, and it has no defect, and they did not output it. And it has a witness on the condition of Muslim, for he cited Sharik ibn Abd Allah al-Nakha'i."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 45 - On the condition of the two; Ibn Rahwayh narrated it from him like this."
"46","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Amr ibn Mansur al-Adl narrated to us: they said: Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali informed us: Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah: from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah: from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: """"Every oath sworn by other than Allah is shirk."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 46 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"47","Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Tuqani narrated to us: Abu Yahya Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Maysarah al-Makki narrated to us. And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar and Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: they said: Bishr ibn Musa informed us. They said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Abu al-Aliyah came to me and a companion of mine, and said: Come, for you two are younger and more retentive of hadith than me. So he went with us until we came to Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi. He said: Narrate to these two your hadith. Nasr said: Uqbah ibn Malik narrated to us, and he was from his tribe. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent a military detachment, so they raided a people. A man from the people strayed, and a man from the detachment followed him with his sword drawn. The stray man said: I am Muslim. He did not pay attention to it, so he struck him and killed him. The news reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he said a severe word, and it reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was delivering a sermon, the killer said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people and continued his sermon. Then he said it a second time: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people and continued his sermon. Then he could not bear but to say it a third time: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned to him, and distress was recognized in his face, then he said: """"Allah Almighty has refused for me the one who kills a believer."""" He said it three times. """"This hadith is output like it in the authentic Musnad of Muslim, for he cited Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah. As for Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi, he is a Companion whose hadith is output in the books of the imams in existence. And I have clarified my condition at the beginning of the book that I output the hadith of the Companions from the last of them, if the path to them is authentic. And Yunus ibn Ubayd has followed Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah in narrating from Humayd on the condition of Muslim."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 47 - On the condition of Muslim."
"48","Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Qadi informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: from Yunus ibn Ubayd: from Humayd ibn Hilal: from Bishr ibn Asim: from Uqbah ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: """"After that, what is the matter with a man who kills a man while he says: I am Muslim?"""" The killer said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said it seeking refuge. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said thus and disliked his statement, and turned his face away from him. Then he said: """"Allah has refused for the one who kills a Muslim, Allah has refused for the one who kills a Muslim."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 48 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"49","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Adami narrated to us, in Baghdad: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Awwam narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammam informed us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Habban al-Ansari informed us: Abu al-Walid and Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us: from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, who said: Shaybah al-Khudari informed me: that he witnessed Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Three things I swear to: Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. The shares of Islam are fasting, prayer, and charity. And Allah does not take charge of a servant then entrust him to other than Him on the Day of Resurrection. And a man does not love a people except Allah makes him with them. And the fourth, if I swore to it, I would hope not to sin: Whatever Allah covers for a servant in the world, He will cover for him in the Hereafter."""" Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: When you hear a hadith like this narrated by Urwah from Aisha, then preserve it. Shaybah al-Hadrami, al-Bukhari output him, and he said in al-Tarikh: And he is called al-Khudari. He heard Urwah and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. And this hadith is authentic in chain and they did not output it."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 49 - Nothing was output for him, meaning Shaybah al-Hadrami, except by al-Nasa'i; this hadith has obscurity in it."
"50","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub al-Faqih narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us. And Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us. And Ali ibn Isa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us. They said: Hushaym narrated to us: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind: from Abi Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad: from Fadalah al-Laythi, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: I want Islam, so teach me some laws of Islam. He mentioned prayer, the month of Ramadan, and the times of prayer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you mention hours in which I am occupied. But teach me a comprehensive statement. He said: """"If you are occupied, then do not be occupied from the two 'Asrs."""" I said: And what are the two 'Asrs? And it was not in my people's language. He said: """"Fajr and Asr."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of Muslim, and they did not output it. In it are wordings they did not output with another chain. Most beneficial of them is the mention of the laws of Islam, for it is in the hadith of Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Dawud, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, and it is not on the condition of one of them. And Hushaym ibn Bashir was contradicted in this chain from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, a contradiction that does not harm the hadith but rather strengthens it."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 50 - On the condition of Muslim."
"51","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us. And Ali ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us. They said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: from Dawud: from Abi Harb: from Abd Allah ibn Fadalah: from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me, and among what he taught me was that he said: """"Guard the five prayers."""" I said: These are hours in which I have occupation. So tell me a comprehensive matter that if I do it, it suffices me. He said: """"Guard the two 'Asrs."""" He said: And it was not in our language. I said: And what are the two 'Asrs? He said: """"A prayer before the rising of the sun, and a prayer before its setting."""" """"And Abi Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili is a major Tabi'i, with him from the major Companions, his hearing from Fadalah ibn Ubayd al-Laythi is not limited. For Hushaym ibn Bashir is a preserver known for preservation, and Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti is a man of a book. And this in general is like what Muslim output in the Book of Faith: the hadith of Shu'bah from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhib, and after him from Muhammad ibn Uthman from his father."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 51 - And Hushaym was contradicted; Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated it from Abi Harb from Abd Allah ibn Fadalah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me."
"52","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi informed me: Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us. They said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us: from Khalid ibn Ma'dan: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Indeed Islam has a light and a minaret like the minaret of the road."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of al-Bukhari, for he narrated from Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani and cited Thawr ibn Yazid al-Shami. As for Khalid ibn Ma'dan's hearing from Abu Hurayrah, it is not far-fetched, for al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated from Thawr ibn Yazid from him that he said: I met seventeen men from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). And perhaps a doubter doubts that this text is anomalous. Let him look in the two Books to find among the anomalous texts that have only one chain what he wonders at, then let him measure this against them. Another hadith with this chain."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 52 - Not far-fetched that Khalid met Abu Hurayrah."
"53","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: from Thawr ibn Yazid: from Khalid ibn Ma'dan: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Islam is that you worship Allah, not associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, enjoin good, forbid evil, and greet your family. Whoever falls short of any of them has left a share of Islam. And whoever leaves all of them has turned his back on Islam."""" """"This hadith is like the first in uprightness."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 53 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"54","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, in Hamdan: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ali informed me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Shall I not teach you - or he said: Shall I not guide you - to a word from under the Throne, from the treasures of Paradise? You say: There is no power and no strength except with Allah. Then Allah Almighty says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."""" """"This hadith is authentic and no defect is preserved for it, and they did not output it. And Muslim cited Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 54 - Authentic, no defect for it."
